cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite the preprint below."
title: "Temperon: sharpness-budget allocation for wall-clock-efficient training"
abstract: >-
  Research code for a study of where to spend an expensive training mode.
  Sharpness-Aware Minimization pays for its second pass only in the final
  anneal: allocating the SAM budget to a scheduled tail reaches full-time-SAM
  quality for roughly a third less wall-clock on three of four vision datasets
  and on a GPT-2-class language model. Includes the negative controls (uniform
  periodic SAM, tail-SAM without a fresh anneal, MSAM) that the claim rests on.
